# [DULT](../wg/dult.html)

## Summary

The Detecting Unwanted Location Trackers (DULT) Working Group held a virtual interim meeting to review the status of active working group drafts and plan next steps toward Working Group Last Call (WGLC). Discussion focused on finalizing `draft-ietf-dult-threat-model`, updates to `draft-ietf-dult-accessory-protocol`, and strategies for documenting existing finding network protocols.

The meeting presentation slides are available in the [Chairs' Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/interim-2026-dult-02/materials/slides-interim-2026-dult-02-sessa-chairs-slides-00).

---

## Key Discussion Points

*   **Threat Model (`draft-ietf-dult-threat-model`)**
    *   Maggie Delano gave an update on `draft-ietf-dult-threat-model`, noting that the document is in good shape. Issues raised on the mailing list (such as family sharing, crowdsourced networks, and multi-network accessories) present valuable considerations, but minor updates to address them do not block overall progress.
    *   Maggie Delano noted there is one open Pull Request (PR) to merge before publishing an updated version.
    *   Sean Turner and Bob Hinden discussed moving the draft to Working Group Last Call (WGLC). Bob Hinden noted that WGLC is an effective way to solicit broader review and that issues can still be resolved if multiple calls are needed.
    *   Sean Turner indicated WGLC for `draft-ietf-dult-threat-model` will likely be issued in approximately one month (following the upcoming IETF meeting).

*   **Accessory Protocol (`draft-ietf-dult-accessory-protocol`)**
    *   Brent Ledvina confirmed he will publish an updated version of `draft-ietf-dult-accessory-protocol` to prevent expiration.
    *   The update will align the document with minor changes in the co-authored industry specification, including adding three new network providers and addressing minor technical adjustments.
    *   Points brought up on the mailing list regarding family sharing and network interactions may be incorporated into this draft where appropriate.

*   **Finding Protocol & Group Roadmap**
    *   Sean Turner recalled that documenting the existing finding network protocol was previously assigned to Eric (Ecker). Sean Turner will follow up to check on availability and next steps for that work.
    *   Brent Ledvina suggested maintaining regular (monthly) virtual interim meetings as a forcing function to keep progress moving forward.

